values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i046$il$, $il$New contact dialog: type to find the company, create it inline, and take both LinkedIn URLs$il$, $il$Lovable UI$il$, $il$Brad$il$, $il$must$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-09T12:29:37.000Z'::timestamptz, 5, '{}'::text[], array[$il$i031$il$]::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${}$il$::jsonb,
$il$Four gaps in the same small dialog. Oliver hit all three on real leads today.

ONE, THE COMPANY PICKER IS A LIST YOU HAVE TO SCROLL, AND IT HIDES THINGS WITHOUT SAYING SO. Oliver hunted for spusu and could not find it. The reason turned out to be that spusu is a Monday company and the picker excludes those. That exclusion is CORRECT, but doing it silently is not: an absent company reads as a missing record, and the obvious next move is to create it again. Show suppressed companies in the results, greyed out, labelled worked in Monday, and not selectable. Then the answer to where is spusu is on the screen instead of being hunted for. It should be a search box: type, and matches appear below. Match on more than the display name, because the display name is often not what someone types. Match the trading name, the legal name, the website domain and the company id, and show country and domain on each result row so near identical entries can be told apart. The record in the screenshot reads Selling Electronics Responsibly FZCO / SER Mobile Phones LLC, which nobody is going to scan for.

TWO, IF THE COMPANY IS NOT THERE THE CONTACT CANNOT BE SAVED AT ALL. Not slower, not clumsier: it does not go in, and Oliver had to abandon a real lead. The search should end with a Create option carrying whatever was typed, so no results flows straight into making the company rather than into a dead end. A company made this way has had no research, so it lands as Untouched with no priority and is visibly marked as created in passing.

THREE, THERE IS ONE LINKEDIN URL FIELD AND THERE SHOULD BE TWO. The dialog takes an /in/ profile. The Sales Navigator /sales/lead/ record is a different thing and it is the one outreach is sent from, while only the /in/ form works for enrichment. Two fields, matching the two columns the lake already holds. This is i031 at the point of entry: if the dialog takes one, every contact created here starts life with the gap we are trying to close.

FOUR, SENIORITY AND FUNCTION ARE FREE TEXT AND SHOULD BE DROPDOWNS. Both are already enums everywhere else. The filter bar behind this dialog counts them: Seniority as C-suite 160, Senior 81, Director 68 and more; Function as Sales 106, Strategy 74, Other 64 and more. Typing them by hand into the create dialog is the one place they can be spelled wrong, and Seniority is read by the sourcing floor, so a typo does not just look untidy, it slips a junior contact past a gate that was meant to catch them. Use the same enum the filters use, do not define a second one.

Raised to a must rather than the nice to have Oliver first called it, because point two is a hard stop on getting data in. Say if you disagree.$il$,
$il$WHY SPUSU WAS HARD TO FIND, corrected by Oliver. Not list length and not spelling. spusu is a MONDAY COMPANY and the picker leaves Monday companies out. The suppression is right. The silence is the bug.

SILENT ABSENCE IS THE MOST EXPENSIVE KIND OF HIDING, because of what the person does next. You look for a company, it is not there, so you conclude it does not exist and you create it. Now there is a duplicate of a company that is in a live Monday deal, and the guard that was protecting it cannot see the new row. The picker prevented one mistake and set up a worse one. Show it, grey it, label it worked in Monday, and let the person read the reason instead of guessing at it.

THE DUPLICATE RISK HERE IS ALREADY REAL. The lake holds THREE spusu records: C456 spusu Austria, C659 spusu Italia, C939 spusu Deutschland GmbH, all marked Monday deal and C939 an Active Lead. A silent picker plus an inline create button is how a fourth gets made. So the create path must check against ALL companies including the suppressed ones, not against the filtered list it is showing.

IT ALSO SHOWS THE SUPPRESSION IS INCONSISTENT RATHER THAN MISSING. The picker honours the Monday flag; the unmatched replies queue in i044 does not. Same rule, two surfaces, two behaviours. Worth finding out which other surfaces honour it before assuming any of them do.

FREE TEXT WHERE AN ENUM EXISTS IS THE SAME DEFECT AS i027, the Countries Selling In field. Worth Brad sweeping the whole app for it once rather than fixing them one screenshot at a time: any field a filter, a score or a guard reads must be a picker, because the number depends on the string matching.

MINIMUM FIELDS ON THE INLINE CREATE: name, website, country. Country because the legality guard reads it and a company with no country cannot safely be drafted to. Everything else waits for research. Do not put a big form in a small dialog.

DUPLICATE CHECK AS YOU TYPE, on the same fields the search matches. Three spusu records already exist, Conrad, getgoods and Voelkner were three, and Save Group and asgoodasnew are probably one group held as two. A create button with no matching behind it is how the fourth appears.

ON THE TWO URLS: neither should be required, because you will not always have both, but the dialog should show which it has and which is missing rather than accepting one silently. A contact with no Sales Nav URL has a dead jump button in i032, and 242 of 665 contacts are already in that state.

A TOOL THAT REFUSES TO STORE WHAT YOU JUST FOUND teaches you to stop putting things in it. The cost is not the two minutes, it is the leads never entered at all, and those are invisible: nobody can count what was abandoned in a dialog. The standing rule is to log every company found, even a non fit, with the reason. This dialog makes that rule impossible to follow at the moment you are trying to follow it.

PAIRS WITH i042 AND i045. All three are the same underlying gap: getting a real person into the system from wherever you found them, without the tool making you do it in the wrong order. Worth Brad treating them as one piece of work.$il$);

