insert into public.improvements (team_id, item_key, title, category, owner, priority, status, raised_by, created_at, build_wave, blocks, blocked_by, done_by, done_at, pinned, hidden, seen_by, detail, notes)
values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i049$il$, $il$The review of what should be a picker and what stays free text, done once$il$, $il$Data & schema$il$, $il$Both$il$, $il$must$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-09T12:52:36.000Z'::timestamptz, 1, array[$il$i027$il$]::text[], '{}'::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${}$il$::jsonb,
$il$Oliver has now hit this five times: Countries Selling In, Seniority, Function, Category, and the general question of which fields should be a selection at all. It is one defect. Fixing it a screenshot at a time means he keeps finding it and Brad keeps making the same change.

Do it as one review. Walk every field on companies and contacts and sort each into three buckets. Already a picker. Genuinely free text, like Notes and Evidence. Should be a picker because something downstream reads it. Then convert the third bucket in one pass and publish the list so nobody has to rediscover it.

The test for the third bucket: does a filter, a score, a guard or a report read this field. If yes it must be a picker, because the answer depends on the string matching. A typo in free text is not untidy, it is a silent wrong number.

Category has a proposed list ready, derived from what is actually in the data. It is in the background below.$il$,
$il$CATEGORY, DERIVED FROM THE REAL DATA rather than invented. The lake holds 16 distinct values across 227 populated rows, and most of the tail is one company each saying the same thing differently:
  Mobile/Gadget Retail 153, Refurb / Recommerce 29, Telco 17, Telco / Manufacturer 9, Software Provider 6, Industry Media / Influencer 2, Consumer electronics retail chain 2, then single instances of B2B IT Leasing / Asset Management, Manufacturer, Software / Telco Infrastructure, Education channel device retail, Department store multi-category retail, Consumer electronics e-commerce, IT / Consumer Electronics Retail, and one row reading Mobile/Gadget Retail with a TBC note inside the value.

SUGGESTED LIST, eight values, argue with it:
  Mobile and gadget retail
  Refurb and recommerce
  Consumer electronics retail, covering the department store, e-commerce and retail chain variants
  Marketplace
  Telco and operator
  Manufacturer and OEM
  IT leasing and asset management
  Software, platform and media
Marketplace is not in the current Category values at all but exists in the other field, and refurbed is one, so it needs to be here. Telco / Manufacturer as a combined value should go: pick the primary and let the group structure in i047 carry the rest.

ONE ROW HAS THE WORD Industry AS ITS CATEGORY VALUE. That is a header row that leaked into the data during a migration. Worth finding, because where there is one there are usually others.

SETTLE CATEGORY AGAINST INDUSTRY FIRST, and the data now proves the overlap rather than just suggesting it. The other field carries Refurbished Specialist, Operator / Manufacturer and Marketplace / Comparison Site, which are the same distinctions in different words. Two pickers for one concept is worse than the free text, because then they can disagree and both look official. Decide whether one of them dies.

INSURANCE PROVIDER IS FREE TEXT AND SHOULD NOT BE. It is on the same screen, and it is the field that names the incumbent carrier: Coverd, Tryg, Wertgarantie, Assurant, Zurich, Ostangler. That is the competitor register in disguise, and it is exactly the field you would want to filter on to ask which carrier we keep running into. As free text it cannot be counted. Same treatment, with the list seeded from what is already recorded plus an other option that flags for review.

OTHER KNOWN MEMBERS OF THE THIRD BUCKET, all raised by Oliver from live screens: Countries Selling In, which is i027 and needs multi select against the canonical country list; Seniority, which the sourcing floor reads, so a typo slips a junior contact past a gate; Function; and the new field in i075 for who the company sells to. Assume there are more. That is the point of reviewing rather than patching.

DO NOT INVENT VOCABULARIES. Where a list already exists, in the filters, the scoring model, or the lake's status vocabulary, use exactly that. A second list that is nearly the same is how values drift apart.

MIGRATION IS THE REAL WORK, not the pickers. Converting a field to an enum leaves every value that does not match, and those become blanks or errors rather than vanishing. Each conversion needs a mapping pass and a reviewed list of what could not be mapped. The unmappable value is often the interesting one.

WHY WAVE 1. These are schema decisions. Changing free text to an enum after things have been written against it is a migration; doing it before is an edit.$il$);

insert into public.improvements (team_id, item_key, title, category, owner, priority, status, raised_by, created_at, build_wave, blocks, blocked_by, done_by, done_at, pinned, hidden, seen_by, detail, notes)
values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i050$il$, $il$Question for Brad: after pressing Send, can I leave the contact and carry on elsewhere?$il$, $il$Outreach & drafting$il$, $il$Brad$il$, $il$question$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-09T12:58:40.000Z'::timestamptz, null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${"Brad": "2026-09-11T08:14:55.532Z", "Oliver": "2026-09-09T13:00:05.343Z"}$il$::jsonb,
$il$When Oliver presses Send now on a draft, does he have to sit on that contact until it completes, or can he navigate away and keep working while it goes?

Two answers needed, and the second is the one that actually matters.
1. Does the UI hold him there. If each send locks the screen for a few seconds, forty sends is several minutes of watching a spinner, and that is the difference between a session that flows and one that does not.
2. If he navigates away mid send, does the touch still get written. A send that completes after the page has moved on, but never records the touch, produces exactly the invisible gap that i048 is about. That would be much worse than a slow spinner.$il$,
$il$WHAT A GOOD ANSWER LOOKS LIKE, so this can be closed properly rather than with a yes.
The send is fired, the card shows sending, and Oliver can move on immediately.
The touch is written by the same operation that sends, not by the page, so navigating away, closing the tab or losing wifi cannot separate the two.
If it fails after he has moved on, it surfaces somewhere he will see it, not only as a toast on a screen he has already left. A failed send that is silently forgotten is the same defect as an unrecorded one.
The contact does not need to be reopened to confirm it went.

WHY OLIVER IS ASKING. The daily pattern is a batch: work down a list of approved drafts and send them one after another. Anything that makes each send a stop rather than a step turns a twenty minute job into an hour, and the thing that gets dropped is the last few sends of the day.

RELATED, NOT THE SAME. i048 is about the timeline being complete. This question is about whether the send flow can break it. If the answer to point two is no, that is not a question any more, it is a must, and it should be raised as one.$il$);
