$il$Yes. Send hands off to the automation and the row updates itself, so you can move on straight away. It takes up to about two minutes: it flips to Scheduled immediately, the phantom sends, and the callback flips it to Sent with the exact text you sent frozen onto the record. If LinkedIn deduplicates it you get a Skipped state with the reason rather than a silent failure, and it stays in Approved so you can decide what to do. You never need to sit and watch it.$il$
